# Fingerprints of secrets that exist in this repo's *git history* only.
# The working tree is clean: every value below has been replaced with a
# placeholder (or, for the test key, generated per session) -- see the
# "Historical findings" note in .gitleaks.toml for the full rationale.
#
# Why this file is needed at all: the Security job checks out with
# fetch-depth: 0, and gitleaks scans the entire history (~38 commits)
# on a manual (workflow_dispatch) or scheduled run rather than only the
# pushed commit range. That's why these surfaced on a manually
# triggered run after a series of green push runs, with no code change
# in between -- different scan scope, not a new leak.
#
# Fingerprint format is <commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>, copied
# verbatim from the gitleaks report. It pins one specific finding, so
# re-introducing any of these values in a new commit produces a
# different fingerprint and still fails the build.
#
# !! These values were publicly readable on GitHub. Suppressing the
# !! alert does not undo the exposure: rotate STEAMPIPE_SERVICE_TOKEN
# !! on any steampipe-service instance where either token was used.

